      <h3 class="type-h2" style="color: var(--color-text-heading);">
        03/ Create a reliable source of truth
      </h3>
      <p class="body-copy">
        <strong>Problem:</strong> Once data was being collected, I needed a
        safe place to store it without losing it. I explored options with
        AI to balance effort and results, then validated the shortlist with
        the IT team since a few AI proposals weren't reliable.
      </p>
      <Accordion
        items={[
          { label: "Exploration 1: Figma memory", value: "before" },
          { label: "Exploration 2: GitHub", value: "after", chosen: true },
          { label: "Exploration 3: RAG Database", value: "option3" },
        ]}
      >
        <div slot="after" class="acc-content-group">
          <div class="pivot-panel">
            <video
              src="/case-studies/design-system-search/pivot3.mp4"
              autoplay
              muted
              loop
              playsinline
              preload="metadata"
            ></video>
          </div>
          <p class="body-copy">
            <strong>Proposal:</strong> Sync the changelog data from the
            plugin to a GitHub repo, stored in <code>.md</code> files
            organised into folders.
          </p>
          <p class="body-copy">
            <strong>Evidence:</strong> No more data overwrites. A "sync
            queue" shows designers what's already on GitHub, so no one gets
            confused. The data also unlocks AI features like search and
            automatic release notes.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div slot="before" class="acc-content-group">
          <div class="pivot-panel pivot-panel-centered pivot-panel-shrink">
            <img
              src="/case-studies/design-system-search/pivot3-before.png"
              alt="Before pivot 3: Figma as source of truth for changelog data"
            />
          </div>
          <p class="body-copy">
            <strong>Proposal:</strong> Store the data directly in Figma
            using shared plugin storage. Zero external infrastructure, and
            fastest to prototype.
          </p>
          <p class="body-copy">
            <strong>Evidence:</strong> Designers couldn't tell what had
            already been shared on Slack, and had no visibility on changes
            made by other designers. On top of that, when multiple
            designers worked at the same time, data got overwritten and
            lost.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div slot="option3" class="acc-content-group">
          <div class="pivot-panel pivot-panel-centered pivot-panel-placeholder">
            <span>Placeholder — RAG database option</span>
          </div>
          <p class="body-copy">
            <strong>Proposal:</strong> A dedicated database with a
            Retrieval-Augmented Generation layer, optimised for semantic
            search. Richest AI features out of the box.
          </p>
          <p class="body-copy">
            <strong>Evidence:</strong> Setup and maintenance cost (schema
            design, hosting, embeddings pipeline) was disproportionate to
            the phase of the project.
          </p>
        </div>
      </Accordion>
